{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model underpredicts the true path in rising regimes. Apply an upward level shift that grows with horizon (small in days 1–5, larger from ~day 10 onward).",
    "Trend/lag error: forecasts react too slowly to upside momentum (true series ramps from high-60s to low-70s while model stays ~68–70). Add a momentum term based on the last 5–10 day slope; if slope > 0, tilt the whole forecast upward, especially mid/long horizon.",
    "Horizon-specific underestimation: largest errors occur around days ~12–25 where true outcomes are ~2–4 EUR above forecast. Use a piecewise correction: +~0.5–1 EUR (days 1–7), +~2–3 EUR (days 8–20), +~1–2 EUR (days 21–30), conditional on positive recent trend.",
    "Insufficient amplitude on rallies: model captures direction but not magnitude during breakouts to 71–73. When price breaks above recent 20–30d range/high, increase projected rally amplitude (scale deviations from baseline by >1).",
    "Over-mean-reversion after strength: model tends to pull back toward ~69–70 even when the true series stays elevated. Reduce mean-reversion strength when spot is above the 20d moving average and the MA is rising."
  ]
}
